Z||000000||87ECO5||06-29-2000||04:14 PM||||Last Sunday, I took the three hour trip to Mid-Ohio (from Southern Ohio).  Once I got on the highway, the "Service Engine Soon" light began flashing every minute or so.  I decided to continue because everything looked OK (oil pressure and temp were fine, engine was running well and not smoking).  Once I got to Columbus, the light stopped flashing.  I went through the entire afternoon at the track without seeing the light.  Jumped back on the highway to head home.  Once I reached Columbus again, the light began flashing again.  It flashed the rest of the way home until I reached my driveway.  Since then, I've not seen the light again (except at startup).<P>I pulled the codes on Monday - 13 and 34.<P>My question is - why did the light stop flashing after Sunday?  Isn't the light supposed to flash continuously (or remain lit) until the problem is corrected (or the computer is reset)?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||06-29-2000||04:49 PM||||<BR>13 is an 02 sensor, 34 is your MAP sensor.<P>If the system locates a problem, the light is to remain on, except if the problem is intermitant, then it can go off again.<P>If your SES light has not come on again, it may be an indication that failure is coming with one or both of those sensors.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||06-29-2000||04:55 PM||||I'm confused (maybe I'm just thick-headed) ...<P>If those sensors are failing, shouldn't the light continue to flash?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Boodoggin||06-29-2000||06:43 PM||||Those sensors are crazy!  Mine only came on above 70mph on bumpy roads<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||dogtired||06-30-2000||05:10 AM||||I have had my cars set several codes.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> When the EGR tube was cracked, causing high idle, the light would come on while sitting at a stop light but them go off when I took off, till I stopped again???<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I think it depends on which system a fault has been found on as to wheather it stays on or goes off??<BR>Fix the indicated problems and see what happens  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Good luck.||||reg||6
Z||000005||lou_dias||06-30-2000||09:33 AM||||My light comed on and stays on til I shut off the car when it is under heavy load like driving over 75 on the highway...<BR>Any ideas?  I smell something too when it is under load.  I have a recent 3.4 rebuild.<BR>Help!||||reg||1
